diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 14584a7..df6637c 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ Dev-only environment variables (see `capture.go`, `app/app.go`, `app/session.go`
 
 **Sign-in sources.** The saved session (`internal/auth`) comes first. If there is none, or it has expired, the app migrates the login of another client on this computer (`internal/migrate`): Baidu's own Linux client first (its Electron cookie store, read with a small pure-Go SQLite reader), then BaiduPCS-Go's active account (`internal/pcsimport`, reading `pcs_config.json`). It skips this when the user signed out on purpose (`settings.SkipImport`). The login screen also offers it as a link. Every sign-in is saved at once, and saved again when `Client.Credentials` changes (the uid found, cookies the netdisk rotated; `Client.OnChange`) and on quit.
 
-**Android client (`android/`).** A second product in the same repository: a Kotlin + Jetpack Compose Material 3 app built with Gradle (AGP 9.4.1, Kotlin 2.4.20, Compose BOM 2026.09.00 with Material 3 1.5.0-rc01 pinned for its public Material 3 Expressive API, compileSdk 37, minSdk 26), entirely separate from `go build`. It shares no code with the desktop app but speaks the same netdisk protocol (the pan.baidu.com web endpoints plus `/api/precreate` → `pcs/superfile2` parts → `/api/create`), the same backup layout and the same `.gpg` format, so the two halves back up into one netdisk folder. `:core` (pure JVM, `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core`) holds `net/BaiduApi` (client, chunked upload, QR sign-in), `crypto/Pgp` (BouncyCastle bcpg; BouncyCastle's v5 session-key quirk had to be turned off for gpg/Go compatibility) and `backup/` (the incremental engine over a `Netdisk` interface and a `BackupSource`, so MediaStore albums and SAF trees are just sources); `:app` (`com.pengstem.baidunetgo`) holds the Compose screens, MediaStore album scanning, the SAF folder picker, Keystore-encrypted storage, WorkManager periodic workers and the foreground backup service. The look is Material 3 Expressive (`MaterialExpressiveTheme` + `MotionScheme.expressive()`, rounded `surfaceBright` cards, expressive switches and segmented rows, a floating tonal navigation bar), following the Material mode of KernelSU rather than its Miuix or liquid-glass variants. `android/docs/CORE-API.md` is the contract between them. Tests: `./gradlew :core:test` runs the client against `cmd/fakepand` (the same `internal/fakepan`, started as a process and its `url=…` line read from stdout; `FAKEPAN_URL` reuses one) and OpenPGP against the real `gpg` in both directions, and `:app:testDebugUnitTest` holds codec/path tests plus Robolectric renders written to `android/screenshots/` (there is no emulator here: no `/dev/kvm`). Builds need `ANDROID_HOME`, `JAVA_HOME` (JDK 21) and a writable `GRADLE_USER_HOME`; `android/keystore/dev.jks` is a public dev-only keystore for `assembleDebug`. `docs/ANDROID.md` is the hand-over (build, CI notes, update-channel idea).
+**Android client (`android/`).** A second product in the same repository: a Kotlin + Jetpack Compose Material 3 app built with Gradle (AGP 9.4.1, Kotlin 2.4.20, Compose BOM 2026.09.00 with Material 3 1.5.0-rc01 pinned for its public Material 3 Expressive API, compileSdk 37, minSdk 26), entirely separate from `go build`. It shares no code with the desktop app but speaks the same netdisk protocol (the pan.baidu.com web endpoints plus `/api/precreate` → `pcs/superfile2` parts → `/api/create`), the same backup layout and the same `.gpg` format, so the two halves back up into one netdisk folder. `:core` (pure JVM, `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core`) holds `net/BaiduApi` (client, chunked upload, QR sign-in), `crypto/Pgp` (BouncyCastle bcpg; BouncyCastle's v5 session-key quirk had to be turned off for gpg/Go compatibility) and `backup/` (the incremental engine over a `Netdisk` interface and a `BackupSource`, so MediaStore albums and SAF trees are just sources); `:app` (`com.pengstem.baidunetgo`) holds the Compose screens, MediaStore album scanning, the SAF folder picker, Keystore-encrypted storage, WorkManager periodic workers and the foreground backup service. It also gains a read-only 文件 browser and a 查重 page mirroring the desktop duplicate finder (`:core`'s `dedup` package: size+MD5 grouping, 按重复组 / 按文件夹 views both foldable, and the same recheck before copies go to the recycle bin). The look is Material 3 Expressive (`MaterialExpressiveTheme` + `MotionScheme.expressive()`, rounded `surfaceBright` cards, expressive switches and segmented rows, a floating tonal navigation bar), following the Material mode of KernelSU rather than its Miuix or liquid-glass variants. `android/docs/CORE-API.md` is the contract between them. Tests: `./gradlew :core:test` runs the client against `cmd/fakepand` (the same `internal/fakepan`, started as a process and its `url=…` line read from stdout; `FAKEPAN_URL` reuses one) and OpenPGP against the real `gpg` in both directions, and `:app:testDebugUnitTest` holds codec/path tests plus Robolectric renders written to `android/screenshots/` (there is no emulator here: no `/dev/kvm`). Builds need `ANDROID_HOME`, `JAVA_HOME` (JDK 21) and a writable `GRADLE_USER_HOME`; `android/keystore/dev.jks` is a public dev-only keystore for `assembleDebug`. `docs/ANDROID.md` is the hand-over (build, CI notes, update-channel idea).
 
 **One keyring key for every build.** `mygo.Secrets` names its service after the build (`<identifier>.dev` under `mygo dev`, the app name under `go run`, the identifier when packaged), so `OpenStore` pins the key to `com.pengstem.baidunetgo`. `auth.Store.Older` lists the old services: `Load` tries their keys and saves the session again under the pinned one.
 
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ Dev-only environment variables (see `capture.go`, `app/app.go`, `app/session.go`
 
 **Duplicate files (`internal/dedup`).** The dedup page reads no file content: `dedup.Scan` walks the folders under a root four at a time (capped at 50,000 files and 5,000 folders, cancelable, reporting progress), and `dedup.Groups` groups what it found by size and MD5, the hash the list API already returns (scrambled there, decrypted in `internal/baidu/list.go` with `baidupcs.DecryptMD5`). Entries with no MD5 are counted and skipped as `缺少哈希，已跳过`; 0-byte files and single files are no group. Groups come by the space freeing all but one copy would free. `app/dedup.go` runs the scan on a goroutine and writes back through `a.update`, throttling progress to about every 180 ms; it keeps the earliest modified copy of each group by default (its path breaking a tie), and `Client.Delete` moves the chosen copies to the recycle bin. Before deleting, it reads the parents' listings again and checks each file still has the scanned fs_id, size and MD5, and that every group keeps a copy; a stale result deletes nothing. The web `filemetas` endpoint is not used to fill in missing hashes.
 
-The page shows the same results in two views: `app/dedup.go`'s `dedupRow` is either a group's heading over its copies (the group view, which the page opens on) or a folder's heading over the copies it holds (the folder view, `dedupState.byFolder`). `flatten` builds the group view's rows, `flattenFolders` the folder view's: a copy is listed under the folder it is in, once, however many other folders its group reaches, each row saying in a chip (with a tip naming them) how many copies and bytes of its group lie elsewhere; folders come by what deleting their spare copies would free, the most first, their path breaking a tie, and their copies keep the group view's order. A folder's line folds its copies away (`dedupState.folded`, by path, in memory only, everything open at first): the click is applied after the list is built, as the rows must not leave while it walks them, and the list is asked to keep the line in view. Both views are only an order of lines: `d.chosen` (by path), `chooseDefaults`, `fullGroup`, `deleteDedup`, `dedupStillThere` and the cache know nothing of the view, so 全选 / 全不选 / 移入回收站 work in either and switching views loses no choice. The cache keeps the groups only, so a restored page opens on the group view; the fold state is not kept.
+The page shows the same results in two views: `app/dedup.go`'s `dedupRow` is either a group's heading over its copies (the group view, which the page opens on) or a folder's heading over the copies it holds (the folder view, `dedupState.byFolder`). `flatten` builds the group view's rows, `flattenFolders` the folder view's: a copy is listed under the folder it is in, once, however many other folders its group reaches, each row saying in a chip (with a tip naming them) how many copies and bytes of its group lie elsewhere; folders come by what deleting their spare copies would free, the most first, their path breaking a tie, and their copies keep the group view's order. A group's heading and a folder's line both fold their copies away (`dedupState.groupFolded`, by key, and `dedupState.folded`, by path, in memory only, everything open at first): a click is applied after the list is built, as the rows must not leave while it walks them, and the list is asked to keep the clicked line in view; switching views keeps each view's folds. Both views are only an order of lines: `d.chosen` (by path), `chooseDefaults`, `fullGroup`, `deleteDedup`, `dedupStillThere` and the cache know nothing of the view, so 全选 / 全不选 / 移入回收站 work in either and switching views loses no choice. The cache keeps the groups only, so a restored page opens on the group view; the fold state is not kept.
 
 Its results are kept between runs in `dedup.json` under the user data dir (`mygo.PathUserData`; tests point `dedupStoreDir` at a temp folder, and the fake netdisk writes nothing), 0600, written atomically (tmp+rename) on a goroutine. The file holds a layout `version`, the account's `uid`, the netdisk `gen` the results describe, the root, `scanned_at`, the statistics and the duplicate groups only — never every scanned file — and reading it back rebuilds the groups (`dedup.Without` regroups them after a delete, so a group of one copy is no group and the order stays by reclaim). `enterDedup` reads and parses it on a goroutine (a few thousand groups), then either fills `dedupState` (`started`, `loaded`, no scan; the header says 上次扫描于 … · 文件未变动，直接显示上次结果) or scans the cached root, else "/". It is valid only while `version` and `uid` match, `gen` equals `App.netdiskGen`, and it is under `dedupCacheAge` (7 days: changes made from another device are not counted here). A scan records the `gen` it started at and writes the cache only if the netdisk did not change meanwhile; else the header says 扫描期间有文件变动，建议重新扫描 and nothing is cached.
 
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index f87b14d..49e8c40 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@
 - 文件浏览器新增剪切 / 复制 / 粘贴（Cmd+X / Cmd+C / Cmd+V）：文件剪贴板只在应用内，跨文件夹移动或复制沿用“复制到…”的同名冲突处理（跳过 / 替换 / 保留两者）；剪切成功后才清空剪贴板，失败、取消或全部跳过时保留可重试，复制则可连续粘贴；剪切到原文件夹、把文件夹粘进自身或子目录会被拒绝，注销时清空。另有 Cmd+A 全选、Cmd+Shift+C 复制网盘路径、Cmd+Shift+V 始终打开系统剪贴板里的分享链接（Cmd+V 在文件剪贴板为空时才这么做）、F5 刷新；右键菜单与状态栏显示剪贴板状态，被剪切的行标出“待移动”，README 增补了快捷键说明。
 - 列表与网格视图按住左键在空白处拖动时显示选择框（弹力框）：半透明强调色填充加 1 像素边框、圆角，随指针移动并选中与矩形相交的行 / 瓦片，松开即消失；预览、对话框、重命名 / 新建文件夹输入中以及把外部文件拖进窗口时不显示。
 
+- 查重「按重复组」视图的组标题也能点击折叠 / 展开：点击组标题收起或展开该组的副本，与「按文件夹」视图各自的折叠状态互不影响（切换视图不丢），组标题上的「保留一份」仍只保留一份、不会顺手折叠该组。
+- Android 客户端新增「文件」与「查重」两个底部标签页：「文件」只读浏览网盘目录（进入子目录、返回上一级、下拉刷新、文件详情含路径 / 大小 / 修改时间 / MD5）；「查重」沿用电脑端逻辑——按大小 + 网盘 MD5 递归扫描整个网盘，支持「按重复组 / 按文件夹」两种视图且两种视图都可折叠，默认每组保留修改时间最早的一份，可全选 / 全不选，移入回收站前重新核对 fs_id / 大小 / MD5 并确保每组留一份；`:core` 新增与桌面 `internal/dedup` 对应的 `dedup` 引擎，并用 `cmd/fakepand` 假网盘做端到端测试。
+
 ### 改进
 
 - Android 端设置页的账号卡片新增头像与会员等级：头像从登录信息 / uinfo 接口取（`http` 的头像地址转成 `https`，Android 9+ 不允许明文加载），圆形显示、没有时用占位图标；会员等级按开放平台的 0/1/2 方案解析（登录接口自有方案如 22=年费 SVIP 作为兜底），名字旁边用金色「SVIP」/色调「VIP」徽章显示。「关于」新增「构建基础」一行，说明基于 pengstem/baidunetgo 的哪个版本、Kotlin + Compose Material 3 Expressive、加密与桌面端同为 OpenPGP。修复 Coil 3 缺少网络模块（`coil-network-okhttp`）导致远程图片（头像、相册封面）静默加载不出的依赖问题。
